# im-operations-hub Git Workflow (Rules)

Commit message wording, staging, validation, and identity live in `AGENTS.md`
(GIT & COMMIT RULES). This rule is the surrounding flow only.
For the full procedure, run the `im-git-workflow` skill.

## 1) Scope

Applies when the user asks for implementation, bugfix, hotfix, release prep,
changelog/version updates, or pull request work in this repository.

Single repo — `origin` is GitHub: `rafadil12/im-operations-hub`.
Module scopes: `report`, `safety`, `training`, `sparepart`, `itsm`,
`organization`, `daily-operation`, `auth`, `employee`, `dashboard`,
`settings`, `db`, `api`, `ui`, `deps`.

## 2) Two gates (mandatory)

**Work gate (default):** implement → validate → normal commit → push → **STOP
for user review**. No version bump. No dated changelog. No `*(release):`
commit. No PR.

**Release gate:** only after the user has reviewed and says `ok release`,
`release`, or `buatkan PR`. Then bump version, write dated changelog, one
`*(release):` commit, push, and create the PR.

Treat `next`, `lanjut`, `commit`, `push`, and follow-up fixes as the work
gate. Do not skip ahead to release.

## 3) Branch mapping (the "base" and the "PR target")

- Normal work: base + PR target `dev`
- Urgent production hotfix, or the user asks for prod-first: base + PR target `main`

After a hotfix is merged to `main`, sync it back into `dev`.

Branch naming (lowercase, hyphen-separated slug):
- major: `release/<x.y.z>`
- feature: `feat/<slug>`
- urgent fix: `hotfix/<slug>`
- non-urgent fix: `fix/<slug>`
- chore: `chore/<slug>`
- refactor: `refactor/<slug>`

Never commit directly to `main` or `dev` unless explicitly told.

## 4) Investigation before changes (for bug reports)

If the user describes a symptom and does NOT explicitly ask to change code:
1. Locate the likely root cause.
2. Summarize with file/area references.
3. Ask: fix on `dev`, or hotfix that targets `main`.

## 5) Versioning and changelog

Sources of truth: `VERSION`, `package.json` `"version"`, `CHANGELOG.md`
(Keep a Changelog 1.1.0, English).

**Work gate:** leave `VERSION` and `package.json` unchanged. Do not create
`## [x.y.z] - YYYY-MM-DD`. Optional Unreleased bullets only if the user asked.

**Release gate** — bump `a.b.c` from current `dev` (or `main` for hotfix):
- user specified `x.y.z` → use it
- major (`a`): breaking/large — bump major, reset minor and patch to `0`
- feature (`b`): new feature — bump minor, reset patch to `0`
- hotfix / fix / chore / refactor (`c`): bump patch

Then move Unreleased notes into `## [x.y.z] - YYYY-MM-DD`. Sections only when
relevant: `Added`, `Changed`, `Deprecated`, `Removed`, `Fixed`, `Security`.
Bullets from the actual diff, not commit logs.

## 6) Push and PR safety

- After a work commit, push unless the user says not to. Never force push.
- Do not open a PR in the work gate. Report branch name, suggested later PR
  title, target branch, and compare URL:
  `https://github.com/rafadil12/im-operations-hub/compare/<target>...<branch>?expand=1`
- Create a PR only in the release gate. Merge only when the user asks to merge.
- Prefer `gh` (`C:\Program Files\GitHub CLI\gh.exe`, user `rafadil12`).

## 7) Commit convention

Follow `AGENTS.md` for staging, validation, and identity.

- Work commits: `<type>(<scope>): <short description>`
- Release commit (release gate only), carrying version + changelog:
  - feature (`b`): `feat(release): v<x.y.z> - <short summary>`
  - hotfix/fix (`c`): `fix(release): v<x.y.z> - <short summary>`
  - chore (`c`): `chore(release): v<x.y.z> - <short summary>`

Keep every subject on one line and under 72 characters.
Never add a `Co-authored-by` trailer or any AI identity.
